      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T17:17:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`SkSurface_Base::onNewCanvas()` returning a bare `SkCanvas*` is a problematic legacy API that we should not propagate. This should accept a `std::unique_ptr\u003cSkCanvas*\u003e` and return a `std::unique_ptr\u003cSkCanvas\u003e`.\n\nIt doesn\u0027t need to return an explicit `SkCaptureCanvas*`, nothing depends on it being fully typed out.  This could also make it so the default implementation just returns the input canvas w/o wrapping if it doesn\u0027t support capturing or capturing isn\u0027t enabled (unless we later on are relying on this returning null to test whether or not capturing is enabled).\n\n\n*edit* I wrote this before outlining the fOwnedCanvas in SkSurface_Base, so the input type doesn\u0027t necessarily need to be `std::unique_ptr\u003cSkCanvas\u003e` if SkCaptureCanvas isn\u0027t owning the base canvas.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 38,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "2a1a838f87c71f11ee6476c5c8e7b74b12759486",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
